WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.100
Bailey: I was attracted to the WHIP program
before even applying to Hillsdale itself.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.100
I first decided to apply to the college, the
whole knowing that they have this fabulous

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:16.820
program that allows you to live, work, and
study in Washington D.C. I can't stay in a

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.430
classroom forever. It's my responsibility
to go out and use my education, so this is

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.400
a wonderful bridge to go out and apply what
I've learned at Hillsdale.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.000
My favorite part about this internship program
is that it forces you to balance. It challenges

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.120
you right from the start. You have to learn
how you're going to get enough sleep every

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:39.350
night so that you can show up and be a responsible
intern, listening to your supervisors, excelling

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.750
at your tasks; but then at night, making sure
that you're prepared for classes and that

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.329
you're ready to engage and talk about the
readings and ask questions.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:51.239
Whenever I have the opportunity to speak to
someone who's interested in the program but

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:56.910
hesitant about spending the time here in D.C.
away from campus, I remind them that, yes,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.940
your Hillsdale experience is valuable. You
may only get four years on the campus or less.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:10.120
You have to remember that Hillsdale is not
confined to the campus. That experience extends further.

